hasimoto@perseus (Kazuhiro Hashimoto FX) writes:

>blank paper. I think that the spellbook is useless, so I always drop it.
>(I have never been able to write in it with a magic marker.)
>Does anyone tell me how to use it?

It IS possible to write scrolls and spells by applying the magic marker
on blank scrolls/spellbooks with the a command.

But you can only write (reliably) scrolls/spells that you already know.
If you try to write something you haven't yet read (or identified with a
scroll/spell of identify), you only have a little chance to succeed.

And a scroll can only be used once, while you can cast a spell several times
and when it wears out, you can read the same spellbook again. So, if you still
have the spellbook, you probably don't need another similar one. Just use
the same one again.
Besides, I have read here that writing spells wears out the marker much
faster than writing scrolls.

So, it is usually more useful to use the marker only for writing scrolls
and ditch or polymorph the blank spellbooks. (Besides, the spellbooks are
quite heavy..)

>How do I kill nymphs and leprechauns?

Don't let the nymphs come too near. Avoid hand-to-hand fights with them,
zap wands and throw things at them instead. If the nymph is beside you,
it is usually best to run away and get at least one empty space between
her and you, then throw a dart or something or zap a wand.

Leprechauns are easier, since they are only interested in money. Drop your
gold before you go bashing them. They don't teleport away so often if you
have no gold in your inventory.

Both nymphs and leprechauns are usually asleep when you find them, and 
they don't do anything before somebody wakens them. So, you can ignore them
as long as they don't move, if you don't want to fight them.
